Theorem RL-14a: non-escaping fixed-size non-unique stack allocation with immortal RC header

  Preconditions:
    - RL-14a governs immortal-header stack promotion per Annex E §AIMS
      Stack Promotion: a non-escaping fixed-size value with Uniqueness !=
      Unique (Locality <= FunctionLocal) SHALL be alloca'd WITH an RC header
      initialized to MAX_REFCOUNT (immortal — prevents a free on the stack
      pointer). Heap children receive field-level RcDec per RL-14.
    - Signature ArcFunction x AimsStateMap -> ArcFunction per
      the canonical proof notation:264; discharged against the sec-01
      Realization.proof sorry obligation.
    - DP-8 (is_local) gates locality; DP-4 (needs_cow_check) explains why the
      header is required: a MaybeShared value may face an IsShared check, and
      a headerless stack value would crash reading a nonexistent header.
    - Shipped: realize/decide.rs Locality consumption; repr.md sec-RH-3.
    - depends-on sec-05: DP-8 (is_local) + DP-4 (needs_cow_check).

  Soundness property:
    Forall fixed-size local value v with Uniqueness(v) != Unique:

      (P1) Strategy decision: RL-14a alloca's v on the stack WITH an immortal
           RC header (MAX_REFCOUNT), for both MaybeShared and Shared.

      (P2) RC soundness: the immortal MAX_REFCOUNT header means (a) an
           IsShared check (DP-4) reads a valid header and never crashes, and
           (b) any RcDec on v is a no-op (the count never reaches 0), so the
           stack pointer is never freed by an RC operation — the stack frame
           deallocates it at scope exit. Heap children are released by
           field-level RcDec per RL-14.

    RL-14a refines plain ARC by keeping the value on the stack (no heap
    allocation) even when its uniqueness is unknown, using the immortal
    header to make RC operations safe no-ops.

  Proof obligation:
    Constructive discharge by the case_analysis engine.

    Part (P1/P2) — non-unique local strategy:
      The verifier asserts that a FunctionLocal fixed-size value with
      Uniqueness in {MaybeShared, Shared} selects ImmortalHeaderStack, and
      that a headerless alternative is rejected (it would crash on IsShared).
      Coverage gate: 2 non-unique cases (MaybeShared + Shared). Negative
      witness: a non-unique local must NOT be headerless.

    Engines dispatched:
      case_analysis (PRIMARY —
        section_08::verify_rl14a_immortal_header_stack; non-unique-local
        strategy enumeration; emits Fail on a wrong strategy or a headerless
        non-unique selection)
      rc_counting (SECONDARY — gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest RL
        row)
      refinement (SECONDARY — gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest RL
        row)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_08 case_analysis engine discharges RL-14a via the non-unique-local strategy decision (MaybeShared + Shared fixed-size locals -> immortal-header stack with MAX_REFCOUNT so IsShared reads a valid header and RcDec is a no-op) with a negative-direction witness rejecting a headerless non-unique local, grounded in repr.md RH-3 + realize/decide.rs Locality consumption
